\f0\b\fs32 \cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Mini Jarvis - Key Files Explained (Current Post Phase 17R)\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf2 Authoritative plain-English guide to the important Mini Jarvis files and how they connect.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 Current State: Stable local AI appliance after Phase 17R\
\
All of your important project files live in:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs20 \cf2 /home/minijarvis/minijarvis\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs26 \cf2 1. Core Application\
jarvis_ui.py\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf2 Purpose:\
This is the main application.\
It handles:\
- GUI window, input box, output display, and overall Tkinter layout\
- Sending prompts to the local AI through the Ollama HTTP API\
- Streaming responses back into the UI\
- Conversation memory\
- /clear command\
- Send button and Enter-to-send behavior\
- Duplicate-send protection while a response is generating\
- Model dropdown for Fast and Deep model selection\
- Status bar showing Ready or Thinking plus the selected model\
- Conversation logging\
- 60-day log cleanup\
- Model metadata in conversation logs\
- Qwen3 thinking suppression through API payload think=False\
- Phase 17R non-fatal logging protection\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 If something feels wrong in GUI behavior, response behavior, model selection, logging, or display behavior, this is usually the first file to inspect.\
\
2. Boot Entry Point (Most Important Startup File)\
start_all.sh\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf2 Purpose:\
This is what turns Mini Jarvis into an appliance.\
It performs:\
- Sets the display environment with DISPLAY=:0\
- Moves into the Mini Jarvis project directory\
- Activates the Python virtual environment\
- Waits briefly for system readiness\
- Warms the default Fast model into memory\
- Launches the GUI by running jarvis_ui.py\
Current important behavior:\
- Only the Fast model is warmed at startup.\
- The Deep model is not preloaded at boot yet.\
- Qwen3 loads later when selected from the GUI Deep mode dropdown.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 This is the single entry point for normal startup.\
\
3. Systemd Service (Boot Automation)\
jarvis.service\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf2 Location:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs20 \cf2 /home/minijarvis/.config/systemd/user/jarvis.service\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs22 \cf2 Purpose:\
Controls:\
- When Mini Jarvis starts\
- How it runs\
- Restart behavior if the GUI exits\
It tells the system:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs20 \cf2 Run start_all.sh automatically at login\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs22 \cf2 This replaced less reliable desktop autostart behavior and is part of the appliance-style boot design.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs26 \cf2 4. AI Models (Managed by Ollama)\
Models are stored internally by Ollama, not inside the project folder.\
Approved GUI Models:\
\
Fast - Qwen 2.5 3B\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs20 \cf2 qwen2.5:3b-instruct-q8_0\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs22 \cf2 Purpose:\
- Default startup model\
- Fast\
- Stable\
- Cool-running\
- Safest appliance default\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 Deep - Qwen 3 8B\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs20 \cf2 qwen3:8b-q4_K_M\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs22 \cf2 Purpose:\
- Selectable from the GUI dropdown\
- Better answers and deeper reasoning\
- Slower and heavier than Qwen2.5\
- Approved only through the HTTP API path with think=False\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 Hidden / Installed but Not Approved in GUI:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs20 \cf2 tinyllama:latest\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs22 \cf2 Reason:\
- Installed but hidden from the GUI dropdown\
- Removed from GUI use because of unstable display behavior and poor prompt-format behavior\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs26 \cf2 5. Ollama Service (System-Level AI Engine)\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf2 Service Name:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs20 \cf2 ollama\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs22 \cf2 Managed by:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs20 \cf2 sudo systemctl status ollama\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs22 \cf2 Purpose:\
- Runs the local AI engine\
- Hosts the local Ollama API\
- Maintains model lifecycle\
- Keeps loaded models available according to keep-alive configuration\
Local API used by Mini Jarvis:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs20 \cf2 http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/generate\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs26 \cf2 6. Ollama Keep-Alive Override\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf2 Location:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs20 \cf2 /etc/systemd/system/ollama.service.d/override.conf\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs22 \cf2 Purpose:\
Keeps loaded Ollama models resident for 24 hours so they do not unload quickly during normal use.\
Current setting:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs20 \cf2 Environment="OLLAMA_KEEP_ALIVE=24h"\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs22 \cf2 Important:\
- This helps keep Qwen2.5 resident after startup.\
- It also allows Qwen3 to remain resident after first Deep-mode use.\
- Do not change this unless a future phase specifically calls for it.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs26 \cf2 7. Python Environment\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf2 Folder:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs20 \cf2 /home/minijarvis/minijarvis/venv\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs22 \cf2 Purpose:\
- Contains all Python dependencies\
- Provides an isolated runtime environment\
- Prevents Python package conflicts with the base operating system\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 Tkinter is provided through operating-system packages, not pip.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs26 \cf2 8. Conversation Logs\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf2 Folder:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs20 \cf2 /home/minijarvis/minijarvis/logs/conversations/\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs22 \cf2 Purpose:\
- Stores local conversation logs\
- Uses one log file per day\
- Includes model metadata for each exchange\
- Maintains a rolling 60-day history\
Daily file format:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs20 \cf2 conversation_YYYY-MM-DD.txt\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs22 \cf2 Retention:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs20 \cf2 60 days\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs22 \cf2 Phase 17R logging policy:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf2 Conversation logging is now best-effort and non-fatal. If log writing fails, Mini Jarvis should still display the model response and continue operating.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 A logging exception may show a warning in the GUI, but it must not break the response flow.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

