\f0\b\fs26 \cf2 12. Current Caution / Editing Discipline\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf2 - Do not edit startup, systemd, or Ollama files unless the current phase specifically requires it.\
- Most GUI behavior changes belong in jarvis_ui.py.\
- Most startup behavior changes belong in start_all.sh.\
- Most boot automation issues belong in jarvis.service.\
- Back up the target file before changing it.\
- Make one focused change at a time.\
- Prefer temp-script patching over fragile inline sed commands.\
- Syntax check after patching.\
- Restart only the necessary service.\
- Validate behavior immediately and report PASS or FAIL.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 13. Key Insight\
You still have a very clean architecture:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf2 - One core app: jarvis_ui.py\
- One startup controller: start_all.sh\
- One system trigger: jarvis.service\
- One local AI engine: Ollama\
- Two approved GUI models: Fast Qwen2.5 and Deep Qwen3\
- One local conversation log area with 60-day cleanup\
- One important Phase 17R safety rule: logging failure must not interrupt a valid model response}